b:
I think that the creation story is just that - a fanciful story, that has so many holes in it that it’s like a sieve.

I love [PERSON] the comedian. He does a really great YouTube video about the creation story as told in [ORGANIZATION]. The beauty of watching this is that it’s not some technical analysis by University professors... it is just down to earth logic and common sense with a huge dose of funny.

Not likely that you will get badly snapped for watching comedy either [PRODUCT];

Lets analyse your fears and see if they are real. You say that all your "friends" are JWs... yet you know that they will shun you and ignore your existence if you stop attending meetings. So these are not true friends, they are robots, controlled by the [ORGANIZATION]. You are losing nothing, but you have an awful lot to gain.

&amp;#x200B;

I left the JWs at [DATE]. I lost a lifetime of these types of friends. I honestly do not miss a single one of them. They were all fakes. I now have friends who truly like me for who I am, and they know the real me. They take the time and effort to keep in touch and engage on more than a superficial (at the meetings) way.

&amp;#x200B;

You are young. Find out who you truly are inside and embrace that person. 

&amp;#x200B;

Do not let fear confine you. You will find heaps of great people if you just get out of the cult prison and allow yourself to grow and develop as a decent human being. You can do this. Look at the [CARDINAL] of people who are on this sub and have done exactly what you are now faced with. They decided to live this life to the full, to follow their passions and dreams and not allow fear, obligation and guilt to turn them into a cult drone. You can do the same!

Look after yourself and especially your brother. You have the knowledge to help him improve his outcomes, so it is important that you do what is right, moral, and decent.

&amp;#x200B;

Your parents need to sort their own lives out, and you need not feel responsible for their choices. That is their concern.

&amp;#x200B;

We each get just [CARDINAL] life... and it is short. There is no dress rehearsal. Live your life as the genuine "you", be true to yourself and your inner moral compass. Do well to your brother and what you know is right. Don't beat yourself up for the flaws of your parents, [CARDINAL] of whom has been sucked into a cult.
